  "lineage": "The one-act, hour-long branch of Spanish lyric theatre that dominated Madrid's Teatro Apolo from the 1870s to about 1910, codified by Federico Chueca ('La Gran Vía', 1886), Tomás Bretón ('La verbena de la Paloma', 1894) and Ruperto Chapí — spoken dialogue alternating with sung numbers built on urban Madrid dance rhythms (chotis, mazurka, habanera, pasodoble, seguidillas), scored for small pit orchestra with prominent clarinet and cornet, chorus of neighbourhood types, and a comic-declamatory vocal style close to speech.",
